1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,022
Lying down at night and feeling that creeping, crawling itch deep in your legs that makes you want to move them, so you can't fall asleep?

2
00:00:08,342 --> 00:00:16,696
Restless legs syndrome is tied to dopamine signaling in the brain, and some everyday foods interfere with that signal or overstimulate your nerves.

3
00:00:17,016 --> 00:00:26,340
Coffee, energy drinks, and even chocolate carry caffeine that overstimulates your nervous system and can block iron absorption, which your brain needs to make dopamine.

4
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:30,276
Try herbal tea instead, or skip caffeine after 2pm.

5
00:00:30,596 --> 00:00:39,920
Wine or beer might make you drowsy at first, but as it wears off later in the night, it can trigger a rebound in nerve activity that makes leg symptoms worse.

6
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:43,440
Try to stop drinking at least 3 to 4 hours before bed.

7
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:51,671
Salty snacks like chips cause fluid retention that can disrupt sleep quality, and poor sleep tends to make restless legs feel worse.

8
00:00:51,991 --> 00:00:54,748
Reach for unsalted nuts or fresh fruit instead.

9
00:00:55,068 --> 00:00:59,765
You don't have to cut all of these out completely - small changes in amount and timing can help.

10
00:01:00,085 --> 00:01:04,643
If you're low on iron, red meat and leafy greens like kale may help too.
